.Dd July 24, 2026
.Dt CAP_XFER_RIGHTS_LIMIT 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cap_xfer_rights_limit ,
.Nm cap_xfer_ioctls_limit ,
.Nm cap_xfer_fcntls_limit
.Nd attenuate descriptor rights during transfer
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/capsicum.h
.Ft int
.Fn cap_xfer_rights_limit "int fd" "const cap_rights_t *rightsp"
.Ft int
.Fn cap_xfer_ioctls_limit "int fd" "const cap_ioctl_t *cmds" "size_t ncmds"
.Ft int
.Fn cap_xfer_fcntls_limit "int fd" "uint32_t fcntlrights"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These system calls set a monotonic ceiling on the authority conveyed when
.Fa fd
is transferred with
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS
or as an attached descriptor in mac_capability messaging.
The sender's descriptor is unchanged.
The received descriptor contains the intersection of the sender's current
capability rights and the transfer ceiling.
.Pp
.Fn cap_xfer_rights_limit
limits the
.Xr rights 4
mask,
.Fn cap_xfer_ioctls_limit
limits the ioctl command allowlist, and
.Fn cap_xfer_fcntls_limit
limits the
.Dv CAP_FCNTL_*
mask.
All three limits can only be tightened.
They are copied by
.Xr dup 2
and
.Xr fork 2
and survive
.Xr execve 2
when the descriptor itself survives.
.Pp
New descriptors initially have an unrestricted transfer ceiling.
Closing the descriptor discards its ceiling.
The ceiling is independent of
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 :
the latter controls whether and how often transfer is permitted, while these
interfaces control the authority received after a permitted transfer.
.Pp
The ioctl and fcntl ceilings are effective only when the rights ceiling
contains
.Dv CAP_IOCTL
and
.Dv CAP_FCNTL ,
respectively.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
These functions fail if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa fd
is not an active descriptor.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
A user address is invalid.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A rights value, ioctl count, or fcntl mask is invalid.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
The requested ceiling would widen an existing ceiling.
.It Bq Er ENOSYS
The kernel was built without
.Cd "options CAPABILITY_MODE" .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_fcntls_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_ioctls_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_rights_limit 2 ,
.Xr cap_xfer_limit 2 ,
.Xr sendmsg 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
These system calls first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
